From 25864a0ffb65b951799badafb1196ad0a0accc02 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 05:05:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] chronik: native protobuf codegen and transport-neutral HTTP
 router

Compile chronik/chronik-proto/proto/chronik.proto, the file the Rust build
uses, into chronik_native_proto with protobuf_generate (Qt's
find_package(Protobuf CONFIG) pattern with the FindProtobuf fallback). The
generated messages are reached as chronik::native::proto (protobuf >= 22
defines a global ::pb namespace).

Add the HTTP layer the handlers plug into, a port of chronik-http's
server.rs routing, error.rs, protobuf.rs and parse.rs semantics:

- HttpRequest/HttpResponse and a Router with ":param" patterns that
  behaves like the axum router the Rust server uses: the protobuf 404
  body, 405 with an Allow header in registration order, HEAD served by
  GET, static segments winning over parameters, the permissive CORS layer
  (-chronikcors) and WebSocket upgrade rejections in axum's order;
- error-to-response mapping (report_status_error): the "NNN: " status
  prefix, "Unknown error, contact admins" for untyped errors, logging of
  5xx;
- protobuf request decoding with the Content-Type checks, body limit and
  error texts of the Rust extractor, including prost's decode-error
  messages (checked against 2,807 cases recorded from prost 0.11.9);
- path and query parameter parsing (heights, hex, LOKAD IDs) with the Rust
  error strings.

Router::Handle may block; transports run it on a query pool, never on
io threads. Handlers themselves come with the query layer.

Tier: eCash

Coordinator integration provenance (metrics369):
Introduce immutable host-neutral request observer and exception-isolation control at the HTTP router first consumer; successful upgrades counted once; native dispatch/header timing boundary documented.
All build/runtime/observer controls deferred by user compile-first policy; ordered source replay is not runtime approval.
